Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a renewed radio's AP Capability Query does not wait for configured siblings

After topology sync a radio waits in ap_cap_query_pending, and the controller
sends the agent's AP Capability Query only when every radio of the agent is
there. When only one radio is renewed (its em_config timed out once, it was
marked misconfigured and AutoConfig Renew re-ran WSC for it alone), its
siblings stay configured and never come back to ap_cap_query_pending: the
renewed radio waits for them until its em_config times out, is renewed again
and waits again, for ever, about every 88 seconds. While it cycles it is never
configured, so it answers no Unassociated STA Link Metrics query and a client
on its band never gets a complete candidate snapshot (seen on rdk-emosa-1002's
wired extender, 2 October: its 2.4 GHz radio cycling, its 5 and 6 GHz radios
configured, the room never settled).

Only a sibling still onboarding (before ap_cap_query_pending) holds the query
now; one past it does not. The radio that sends the query is elected among the
radios waiting for it, since a configured sibling may be executing another
command. The report still moves every radio that waits for it.

The same wait one step earlier, at the Topology Query, is the patch before
this one.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
+++ b/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
@@ -1780,16 +1780,26 @@
                 std::vector<em_t *> em_radios;
                 dm_easy_mesh_t *dm = get_data_model();
                 get_mgr()->get_all_em_for_al_mac(dm->get_agent_al_interface_mac(), em_radios);
+                em_t *query_em = NULL;
                 for (auto &em : em_radios)
                 {
-                    if (em->get_state() != em_state_ctrl_ap_cap_query_pending){
-                        em_printfout("radio %s is not in AP Capability query pending state, ignoring",
-                                     util::mac_to_string(em->get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str());
+                    // Only a sibling still onboarding (before this query) holds it. One
+                    // already past it, because it finished earlier and only this radio was
+                    // renewed, must not: waiting for it times this radio's em_config out,
+                    // renews it and waits again, for ever.
+                    if (em->get_state() < em_state_ctrl_ap_cap_query_pending){
+                        em_printfout("radio %s is in state:%d, before the AP Capability query, ignoring",
+                                     util::mac_to_string(em->get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str(), em->get_state());
                         em_radios.clear();
                         return;
                     }
+                    // The radio that sends the query is elected among the radios waiting
+                    // for it: a sibling already past it may be executing another command.
+                    if ((query_em == NULL) && (em->get_state() == em_state_ctrl_ap_cap_query_pending)) {
+                        query_em = em;
+                    }
                 }
-                if (this == em_radios.front()){
+                if (this == query_em){
                     em_printfout("Sending the AP query message to agent al_mac:%s on radio: %s",
                         util::mac_to_string(dm->get_agent_al_interface_mac()).c_str(),
                         util::mac_to_string(get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str());
